IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `spr-dates`
IMPORT `spr-part1-general`

-- State Pension Regulations 2015 (S.I. 2015/173), revised text at 2026-04-06.
--
-- LAYER 1, PART 5 AND THE SCHEDULE: regulation 14 and the Schedule (amendments to other
-- legislation relating to the sharing of state pension rights on divorce or the
-- dissolution of a civil partnership).
-- Written from the text alone and from no one's point of view.
--
-- Most of the Schedule is a list of textual amendments to two other sets of
-- regulations (the Sharing of State Scheme Rights (Provision of Information and
-- Valuation) (No.2) Regulations 2000 and the Pensions on Divorce etc. (Pension
-- Sharing) (Scotland) Regulations 2000). Those words are INERT here: they decide
-- nothing until read into the amended instruments, which are not among the inputs.
-- The one exception is paragraph 1(10), which inserts a new Part 3 into the 2000
-- Regulations. Its regulations 6 and 7 say what the Secretary of State must give
-- a person (or the court, or the person's spouse) and by when; they are encoded below
-- under the numbers they carry in the amended instrument ("inserted regulation 6").
--
-- Regulation 1(3) lifts the 6 April 2016 cut-off for Part 5, so nothing here is gated
-- on the person's pensionable age (spr-part1-general.l4,
-- `regulation 1(3): Part 5 applies to the person`).
-- "Relevant date" has the meaning of section 10(3) of the Family Law (Scotland) Act 1985
-- (inserted regulation 1(2) definition, in the Schedule): it exists only in Scottish
-- proceedings and is taken as a plain input date.

§ `Part 5: Amendments to other legislation`

§§ `Regulation 14: sharing of state pension scheme rights`

-- Regulation 14 only gives effect to the Schedule ("has effect"). It decides nothing
-- for a person, so it is inert.

§§ `Inserted regulation 6(1): what the Secretary of State must furnish, and to whom`

DECLARE WhoRequests IS ONE OF
    `the person who has shareable new state scheme rights`
    `the court, by an order`
    `the spouse or civil partner of the person who has shareable new state scheme rights`

DECLARE InformationToBeFurnished IS ONE OF
    `the information in paragraphs (2) to (6)`
    `the information in paragraph (6) only`

-- Gloss: the person themselves (on request) and the court (on an order) are entitled to
-- the valuation information and the explanation; the spouse or civil partner only to
-- the explanation in paragraph (6).
-- src:545 | (1) The requirements imposed on the Secretary of State for the purposes of section 23(1)(a) of the 1999 Act (supply of pension information in connection with divorce etc.) are that he shall furnish—
-- src:546 | (a) the information specified in paragraphs (2) to (6)—
-- src:547 | (i) to a person who has shareable new state scheme rights on request from that person; or
-- src:548 | (ii) to the court, pursuant to an order of the court; or
-- src:549 | (b) the information specified in paragraph (6) to the spouse or civil partner of a person who has shareable new state scheme rights, on request from that spouse or civil partner.
@ref Inserted regulation 6(1) (src:545-549)
GIVEN who IS A WhoRequests
GIVETH A InformationToBeFurnished
`inserted regulation 6(1): the information the Secretary of State must furnish` who MEANS
    CONSIDER who
    WHEN `the person who has shareable new state scheme rights` THEN `the information in paragraphs (2) to (6)`
    WHEN `the court, by an order` THEN `the information in paragraphs (2) to (6)`
    WHEN `the spouse or civil partner of the person who has shareable new state scheme rights` THEN `the information in paragraph (6) only`

§§ `Inserted regulation 6(2) to (5): which valuation`

DECLARE ValuationGiven IS ONE OF
    `a valuation of the shareable new state scheme rights as at the date the request is received`
    `a valuation of the shareable new state scheme rights as at the relevant date`
    `a valuation of the previous shareable old state scheme rights as at the relevant date`

-- Gloss: the default is a valuation as at the day the request arrives (2). Where there is
-- a "relevant date" (the date fixed in Scottish proceedings), the valuation is as at
-- that date: of the new rights if that date is on or after 6 April 2016 (3); of the
-- previous old rights if it is before 6 April 2016 and the request arrives on or after
-- that day (4).
-- The inserted regulation takes effect from 6 April 2016 (regulation 1(2)); a request
-- received before that is outside it, and the answer is NOTHING.
-- src:550 | (2) Except where paragraphs (3) or (4) apply, the information specified in this paragraph is a valuation of the person's shareable new state scheme rights as at the date of receipt of a request for such a valuation.
-- src:551 | (3) The information specified in this paragraph is a valuation of the person's shareable new state scheme rights as at the relevant date, where the relevant date is on or after 6th April 2016.
-- src:552 | (4) The information specified in this paragraph is a valuation of the person's previous shareable old state scheme rights as at the relevant date, where the relevant date is before 6th April 2016 and the request for a valuation is received on or after 6th April 2016.
@ref Inserted regulation 6(2) to (4) (src:550-552)
GIVEN `the relevant date, if there is one` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the Secretary of State receives the request` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE ValuationGiven
`inserted regulation 6(2) to (4): the valuation to be given` `the relevant date, if there is one` `the date the Secretary of State receives the request` MEANS
    IF `the date the Secretary of State receives the request` LESS THAN `regulation 1(2): the commencement date`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the relevant date, if there is one`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST `a valuation of the shareable new state scheme rights as at the date the request is received`
         WHEN JUST relevantDate THEN
             IF relevantDate AT LEAST `regulation 1(2): the commencement date`
             THEN JUST `a valuation of the shareable new state scheme rights as at the relevant date`
             ELSE JUST `a valuation of the previous shareable old state scheme rights as at the relevant date`

-- Gloss (5): where the relevant date is before 6 April 2016 and the request arrives on or
-- after that day, the person may also ask for the amount of their former entitlement to
-- a Category A retirement pension (by virtue of section 44(3)(b) of the 1992 Act).
-- src:553 | (5) The information specified in this paragraph is the amount of the person's former entitlement to a category A retirement pension by virtue of section 44(3)(b) of the 1992 Act as at the relevant date and immediately before 6th April 2016, where the relevant date is before 6th April 2016 and the request for information about that amount is received on or after 6th April 2016.
@ref Inserted regulation 6(5) (src:553)
GIVEN `the relevant date, if there is one` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the Secretary of State receives the request` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`inserted regulation 6(5): the amount of the former Category A entitlement may be given` `the relevant date, if there is one` `the date the Secretary of State receives the request` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the relevant date, if there is one`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST relevantDate THEN
            relevantDate LESS THAN `regulation 1(2): the commencement date`
        AND `the date the Secretary of State receives the request` AT LEAST `regulation 1(2): the commencement date`

§§ `Inserted regulation 6(7) and (8): by when`

DECLARE InformationRequest HAS
    `who makes the request or order` IS A WhoRequests
    `the date the Secretary of State receives the request or order` IS A DATE
    `the request or order asks for a valuation under paragraphs (2) to (4) or an amount under paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person notified the Secretary of State by that date that the information is needed in connection with proceedings under a provision referred to in section 23(1)(a) of the 1999 Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the last day of any shorter period the court has specified in an order, if any` IS A MAYBE DATE

-- Gloss (8): one month from the day the request arrives, where a request or order from
-- the person or the court does not ask for a valuation or amount, or where the spouse or
-- civil partner asks for the paragraph (6) information.
-- "One month beginning with" a date is counted by convention F2.
-- src:563 | (8) Where—
-- src:564 | (a) the request made by the person with shareable new state scheme rights for, or the court order requiring, the provision of information does not include a request or, as the case may be, an order for a valuation under paragraphs (2), (3) or (4) or an amount under paragraph (5); or
-- src:565 | (b) the spouse or civil partner of the person with shareable new state scheme rights requests the information specified in paragraph (6),
-- src:566 | the Secretary of State shall furnish that information to the person who has shareable new state scheme rights, that person's spouse or civil partner, or the court, as the case may be, within one month beginning with the date the Secretary of State receives the request or the court order for the provision of that information.
@ref Inserted regulation 6(8) (src:563-566)
GIVEN request IS A InformationRequest
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`inserted regulation 6(8): the one-month period applies` request MEANS
        request's `who makes the request or order` EQUALS `the spouse or civil partner of the person who has shareable new state scheme rights`
    OR NOT (request's `the request or order asks for a valuation under paragraphs (2) to (4) or an amount under paragraph (5)`)

-- Gloss (7): otherwise three months from the day the request arrives; six weeks where
-- the person told the Secretary of State by then that the information is needed for
-- proceedings already commenced; or any shorter period the court has set. The three
-- are alternatives joined by "or" and the earliest limit that applies is taken
-- (fork F18). "Beginning with" a date: conventions F1 and F2.
-- src:559 | (7) The Secretary of State shall furnish the information specified in paragraphs (2) to (6) to the court, or, as the case may be, to the person who has shareable new state scheme rights within—
-- src:560 | (a) three months beginning with the date the Secretary of State receives the request or, as the case may be, the order for the provision of that information;
-- src:561 | (b) six weeks beginning with the date the Secretary of State receives the request or, as the case may be, the order for the provision of the information, if the person who has shareable new state scheme rights has notified the Secretary of State by the date the Secretary of State receives the request or order that the information is needed in connection with proceedings commenced under any of the provisions referred to in section 23(1)(a) of the 1999 Act; or
-- src:562 | (c) such shorter period specified by the court in an order requiring the Secretary of State to provide a valuation in accordance with paragraphs (2), (3) or (4) or an amount in accordance with paragraph (5).
@ref Inserted regulation 6(7) (src:559-562)
GIVEN request IS A InformationRequest
GIVETH A DATE
`inserted regulation 6(7): the last day for furnishing the information` request MEANS
    `the earlier of` withNotification `and` withCourt
    WHERE
        received MEANS request's `the date the Secretary of State receives the request or order`
        threeMonths MEANS `the last day of a period of months starting on` received 3
        sixWeeks MEANS `the last day of a period of days starting with` received 42
        withNotification MEANS
            IF request's `the person notified the Secretary of State by that date that the information is needed in connection with proceedings under a provision referred to in section 23(1)(a) of the 1999 Act`
            THEN `the earlier of` threeMonths `and` sixWeeks
            ELSE threeMonths
        withCourt MEANS
            IF request's `who makes the request or order` EQUALS `the court, by an order`
            THEN CONSIDER request's `the last day of any shorter period the court has specified in an order, if any`
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN withNotification
                 WHEN JUST courtEnd THEN `the earlier of` withNotification `and` courtEnd
            ELSE withNotification

@ref Inserted regulation 6(7) and (8) (src:559-566)
GIVEN request IS A InformationRequest
GIVETH A DATE
`inserted regulation 6(7) and (8): the last day by which the Secretary of State must furnish the information` request MEANS
    IF `inserted regulation 6(8): the one-month period applies` request
    THEN `the last day of a period of months starting on` (request's `the date the Secretary of State receives the request or order`) 1
    ELSE `inserted regulation 6(7): the last day for furnishing the information` request

§§ `Inserted regulation 7: how the valuation is calculated and verified`

-- Gloss: where an application for financial relief or provision (on divorce or
-- dissolution) has been made, or is in contemplation, the valuation is calculated and
-- verified in accordance with the Government Actuary's guidance.
-- src:568 | Where an application for financial relief or financial provision under any of the provisions referred to in section 23(1)(a) of the 1999 Act has been made or is in contemplation, the valuation of shareable old or new state scheme rights shall be calculated and verified for the purposes of regulation 6(2) to (4) of these Regulations in accordance with guidance from time to time prepared by the Government Actuary.
@ref Inserted regulation 7 (src:568)
GIVEN `an application for financial relief or financial provision has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `such an application is in contemplation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`inserted regulation 7: the valuation is calculated and verified in accordance with the Government Actuary's guidance` `an application for financial relief or financial provision has been made` `such an application is in contemplation` MEANS
    `an application for financial relief or financial provision has been made` OR `such an application is in contemplation`
